<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.1 Moral Vulnerability Does Not Decline with Capability ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Moral baseline accuracy remains near chance.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.1 Moral Vulnerability Does Not Decline with Capability ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Moral vulnerability does not decline with capability.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.1 Moral Vulnerability Does Not Decline with Capability ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Alternative explanation: task difficulty.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS1.SSS0.Px4" title="In 4.1 Moral Vulnerability Does Not Decline with Capability ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Alternative explanation: item ambiguity.</span></a></li>
