Directional Selectivity</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" title="In 4.3 Simple Prompting Cannot Restore Directional Selectivity ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Explicit reasoning amplifies compliance symmetrically.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" title="In 4.3 Simple Prompting Cannot Restore Directional Selectivity ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Traces reveal rationalization, not deliberation.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" title="In 4.3 Simple Prompting Cannot Restore Directional Selectivity ‣ 4 Results ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Instruction-based prompting suppresses compliance but cannot redirect it.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S5" title="In Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">5 </span>Discussion</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 5 Discussion ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The target for alignment.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 5 Discussion ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Why moral directionality is harder.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S5.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 5 Discussion ‣ Right or Wrong, Models Comply: Directional Blindness in LLM Moral Judgment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Implications for evaluation.</span></a></li>
